; positive control for iff-third-attempt-blocks-eigenvariable.kurt: confirms the fix (blocking
; the goal's own free variables before `impl_elim`'s `is_iff` "third attempt" direct match)
; doesn't overcorrect into breaking genuine `not-not`/`iff` reasoning where there's nothing
; unsound going on -- either because the goal has no free variables of its own, or because a
; free variable is legitimately protected (as a fixed constant, not eligible for unification)
; by an enclosing `let`.
load propositional
prop P
use P

; a goal with no free variables of its own: blocking an empty set is a no-op
not (not P)
P iff (not (not P))

; a statement constant is a genuine constant (not free-for-unification) -- so the third-attempt
; match against `not-not` still fires directly (no other axiom involved, so the reason below can
; only be "not-not", not some other, confounding fact). (Until 2026-10-20 this was a `let x` over a
; statement variable; `let` fixes a term only since then.)
prop x
x iff (not (not x))
true
